You can create a vector of integers in C++ using the `std::vector` class template. To initialize the vector to a specific value `c`, you can use the `resize()` function to set the size of the vector to `c`, and then use the `fill()` function to set all the elements to the value `c`. Here's an example:
```css
#include <vector>

int main() {
    std::vector<int> v(5); // create a vector of size 5
    v.resize(5); // resize the vector to 5 elements
    v.fill(5); // set all elements to 5
    return 0;
}
```
In this example, a `std::vector` of size 5 is created, and then resized to 5 elements. Finally, all the elements are set to the value 5 using the `fill()` function.

